# libadrenotools' hook loads a custom driver uniquely when its soname is taken. The driver's namespace is a clone of the
# vendor one, so when a library with the driver's soname is in the process already (vulkan.adreno.so: Android 16 loads
# the system's driver as the app starts), bionic hands that one back by soname and the package is never opened, which
# Qualcomm's own packages hit. On that collision the hook copies the package into <customDriverDir>/unique/ with each
# library renamed by flipping the case of the last letter before ".so" (vulkan.adreno.so is vulkan.adrenO.so) and
# DT_SONAME, DT_NEEDED and the verneed names rewritten in place, at the same length, and loads it from there. Without
# a collision the hook runs as released. The same change rEden carries (its .patch/libadrenotools/0002).
#
# cmake/adrenotools.cmake applies it to a copy of the release and checks the result. To change it, edit a copy of the
# release's src/hook/hook_impl.cpp and regenerate this diff, then the hash in cmake/adrenotools.cmake.

